docs {
  # Skills — packaged expertise, and each person's own credentials

  A skill is a folder holding `SKILL.md` (YAML frontmatter + markdown), optionally with
  `references/` and `scripts/`. It is the open Agent Skills format Claude Code and GitHub
  Copilot both read, so a skill written for either works here unmodified.

  Two tiers, because they are genuinely different acts:

  * **Using** one is open to everybody, and so is supplying **your own** credentials for it.
  * **Installing / removing / re-scoping** one is **admin only** — a skill may bundle scripts,
    and a script runs with the server's own privileges.

  A skill whose scripts read credentials is registered as **user-scoped** on arrival: it will
  not run until the calling person supplies those values, and it never falls back to whatever
  the server happens to hold under the same names. So `GET /api/skills` answers "is this ready
  **for me**", not "does this exist".

  Secrets are encrypted at rest and **write-only**: no endpoint anywhere reads a value back
  out, so the list request returns names only.

  Set `skillZip` (a .zip containing SKILL.md), `skillName` and `skillSecretKey` in the
  environment before running this folder.
}
